window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-d6b5aa6a43ce8c0f"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"use-chatgpt\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"chatgpt\">使用 ChatGPT</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"go-from-idea-to-useful-result\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">从想法到有用的结果</h2> <p>ChatGPT 是一种 AI 智能体，你可以用日常语言与它交流：</p> <ol> <li> <p>从一个问题、想法、粗略笔记、文件或待完成的任务开始。</p> </li> <li> <p>请 ChatGPT 解释信息、拓展想法、起草内容、研究主题、分析材料，或创建新内容。</p> </li> <li> <p>提供它需要的背景和工具，例如文件、网页搜索、项目或插件。</p> </li> <li> <p>检查结果、纠正方向，并要求修改。你的第一条提示不必完美，也不需要特殊命令。</p> </li> </ol> <p><a id=\"choose-how-you-want-to-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">选择适合你的工作方式</h2> <p>如果你想提问或来回讨论，请使用 Chat。若希望 ChatGPT 把较大的任务推进到可供审阅的结果，请在切换器中打开 Work。如果你需要开发者视图或更详细的技术信息，尤其是软件开发方面的信息，请选择 Codex。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>选择</th> <th>适用场景</th> <th>示例</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Chat</td> <td>与 ChatGPT 一起逐步讨论</td> <td>提问、网页搜索、头脑风暴、起草消息、比较选项</td> </tr> <tr> <td>ChatGPT Work</td> <td>明确目标并获得可审阅的结果</td> <td>创建演示文稿、分析文件、起草报告、制定项目计划</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex</td> <td>使用开发者工具并查看技术细节</td> <td>调试代码、运行测试、审查 PR、实现功能</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>你可以用 Chat 提问、头脑风暴、起草或修改文本、总结文件、比较选项，或厘清较复杂的事情。在 Codex 中，选择 <strong>New chat</strong>，然后在有此选项时选择 <strong>Quick chat</strong>。</p> <p>如果需要一个完整、可供审阅的成果，请切换到 <strong>Work</strong>，并描述你希望成果包含什么。示例任务、提示和最佳实践请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-2c7688c996bc9669\">开始使用 ChatGPT Work</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"what-chatgpt-work-can-do\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"chatgpt-work\">ChatGPT Work 可以做什么</h3> <p>ChatGPT Work 可以规划任务、收集上下文、使用工具，并持续完成工作，直到得到可供你审阅的结果。</p> <blockquote> <p>图示：ChatGPT Work 对比供应商并制作可供审阅的电子表格</p> </blockquote> <p>你可以请它：</p> <ul> <li><strong>研究和分析信息。</strong> 搜索网页、浏览网站、比较来源、读取文件、分析数据并总结发现。</li> <li><strong>使用你的文件和工具。</strong> 使用上传的文件、<a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">项目</a>、记忆、ChatGPT Library 和已安装的<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a>。插件可以提供已连接信息、可重复使用的工作流和受支持的操作。</li> <li><strong>创建完整文件。</strong> 起草并润色<a href=\"#/article/a-1186da4cb8c2d6e2\">文档、演示文稿、电子表格和 PDF 文件</a>。检查结果、提出具体修改，并下载完成的文件。</li> <li><strong>创作视觉和互动内容。</strong> 生成或编辑<a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">图片</a>，创建互动式<a href=\"#/article/a-989576428b6123b7\">可视化内容</a>，并使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Sites</a> 创建或分享网站和应用。</li> <li><strong>跨网站和应用工作。</strong> 使用<a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809\">浏览器</a>研究网站并与其交互。在桌面应用中，如果这些功能可用，还可以使用<a href=\"#/article/a-a7459570776840aa\">浏览器扩展程序</a>、<a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use</a> 和 <a href=\"#/article/a-c302b8efa03eab38\">appshots</a>。</li> <li><strong>运行代码并审查技术工作。</strong> 运行代码和 Shell 命令、分析数据、检查文件、<a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">审查代码</a>，并使用所选环境可访问的代码库开展工作。</li> <li><strong>分派任务并继续长期工作。</strong> 将相互独立的工作拆分给<a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">子智能体</a>，跟进进度，并保持<a href=\"#/article/a-916e12c5bba5b9cc\">长期运行的工作</a>持续推进。</li> <li><strong>重复使用有效工作流。</strong> 设置<a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">计划任务</a>，并通过<a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">技能</a>复用工作流。</li> <li><strong>通过对话讨论任务。</strong> 在支持的套餐和桌面应用中，使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-3b6d55bd01328040\">ChatGPT Voice</a> 开始工作、检查进展或调整方向。</li> </ul> <p>功能可用性取决于套餐、平台、地区、推出范围和工作区设置。工作区管理员可以控制 ChatGPT Work、插件、浏览器和网络访问。ChatGPT Work 与 Codex 共用<a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">使用限额</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-cloud-or-local-work\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">选择云端或本地工作</h3> <p>在网页版中，ChatGPT Work 在托管云环境中运行。在桌面应用中，你还可能可以选择任务运行的位置：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Cloud：</strong> 在隔离的托管环境中运行工作。即使关闭桌面应用，任务也可以继续运行，并能在网页或移动应用中继续处理。云端工作可以使用上传文件、已连接工具和获准网站。</li> <li><strong>Work locally：</strong> 使用电脑上的文件、应用或浏览器。如果账户或工作区已启用此功能，就可以在桌面应用中本地工作。</li> </ul> <p>ChatGPT 会显示进度，并在需要信息或审批时暂停。批准重大操作前请先检查，使用或分享最终结果前也请核实。</p> <p><a id=\"compare-work-mode-and-codex-on-desktop\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"compare-chatgpt-work-and-codex-on-desktop\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"chatgpt-work-codex\">比较桌面应用中的 ChatGPT Work 与 Codex</h3> <p>ChatGPT Work 与 Codex 的能力有重叠。如果你更喜欢 Codex，仍可用它进行研究、文档、演示文稿和其他知识工作。如果两者都可用，桌面应用的界面和智能体呈现工作的方式会有所不同。</p> <p><strong>详细比较</strong></p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>差异</th> <th>桌面应用中的 ChatGPT</th> <th>桌面应用中的 Codex</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>从哪里开始</td> <td>选择 <strong>ChatGPT</strong>，然后切换到 <strong>Work</strong></td> <td>在产品选择器中选择 <strong>Codex</strong></td> </tr> <tr> <td>可见的对话</td> <td>可查看从网页和移动端 Chat 开始的对话，以及 ChatGPT Work 对话</td> <td>主要显示 Codex 对话和开发项目</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Quick chat</td> <td>不提供</td> <td>在可用时，可以在 Codex 中访问从网页和移动端开始的 ChatGPT 对话</td> </tr> <tr> <td>技术细节</td> <td>隐藏 Git 或 Shell 命令等技术细节</td> <td>查看差异和审查视图等开发者细节</td> </tr> <tr> <td>智能体的沟通方式</td> <td>倾向于使用非技术语言并提供完整成果</td> <td>可以包含技术细节和实现过程</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Pull requests 窗格</td> <td>使用 ChatGPT Work 时不提供</td> <td>启用后可用</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"talk-to-chatgpt-naturally\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"chatgpt_1\">自然地与 ChatGPT 对话</h3> <p>把请求说得像是在向一位乐于助人的同事解释一样。说明你想完成什么、哪些细节会影响答案，以及你需要什么格式。第一条提示只是起点；你可以继续补充背景或改进结果。</p> <p><strong>从简单请求开始：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Help me plan a 30-minute team meeting about our new customer feedback process.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">帮我规划一次 30 分钟的团队会议，主题是我们新的客户反馈流程。</div></div> <p>（中文：请帮我规划一次 30 分钟的团队会议，主题是我们新的客户反馈流程。）</p> <p><strong>补充背景：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Help me plan a 30-minute team meeting about our new customer feedback process. The audience is a customer support team that hasn't seen the process before. Include five minutes for questions and end with clear next steps.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">帮我规划一次 30 分钟的团队会议，主题是我们新的客户反馈流程。受众是尚未了解该流程的客户支持团队。留出五分钟用于提问，并以明确的后续步骤收尾。</div></div> <p>（中文：请帮我规划一次 30 分钟的团队会议，主题是我们新的客户反馈流程。参会者是一个还不了解此流程的客户支持团队。请留出五分钟提问，并以明确的后续步骤结束。）</p> <p><strong>指定格式：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Create a 30-minute agenda for a customer support team that hasn't seen our new customer feedback process before. Include five minutes for questions, end with clear next steps, and format it so I can paste it into a calendar invitation.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">为尚未了解我们新客户反馈流程的客户支持团队，制作一份 30 分钟的会议议程。留出五分钟用于提问，以明确的后续步骤收尾，并采用方便我粘贴到日历邀请中的格式。</div></div> <p>（中文：为一个尚未了解我们新客户反馈流程的客户支持团队，制作一份 30 分钟会议议程。留出五分钟提问，以明确的后续步骤结束，并按照可直接粘贴到日历邀请中的格式编排。）</p> <p>你还可以继续提出简单要求，例如：</p> <ul> <li>“把这段写得更短。”</li> <li>“给我三种不同的方案。”</li> <li>“你做了哪些假设？”</li> <li>“继续之前先问我几个问题。”</li> </ul> <p>要了解更多信息，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64\">提示指南</a>，或参加 <a href=\"https://academy.openai.com/home/courses/ai-foundations-juzjs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AI 基础课程（需联网）</a>进行系统练习。</p> <p><a id=\"bring-the-right-context-into-chatgpt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt_2\">为 ChatGPT 提供恰当的上下文</h2> <p>向 ChatGPT 提供与任务相关的信息、工具和指示。你不需要把所有内容都提供给它，只需包括那些会影响理想结果的上下文。</p> <p><a id=\"keep-related-work-in-a-project\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">将相关工作放在项目中</h3> <p>项目可以帮助你围绕某个主题、目标或持续进行的工作来组织 ChatGPT。如果工作会长期继续，或需要依赖同一批上下文，请将相关对话、文件和指示放在一个项目中。<a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">了解项目</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"attach-files\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">附加文件</h3> <p>你可以上传或附加文档、演示文稿、电子表格、PDF 文件、图片和数据导出文件。以下情况可以使用这些文件：</p> <ul> <li>总结或比较文件。</li> <li>查找模式或不一致之处。</li> <li>提取、清理或重新整理信息。</li> <li>将文件用作创建新文件的源材料。</li> </ul> <p>ChatGPT 创建文件后，请打开预览并检查内容。然后你可以继续要求修改，不必从头开始。有关<a href=\"#/article/a-1186da4cb8c2d6e2\">使用文件</a>的更多信息，请参阅相应文档。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-tools-with-plugins\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">通过插件连接工具</h3> <p>插件可以将 ChatGPT 连接到你工作中使用的工具和信息来源，例如 Google Drive、SharePoint、Salesforce 或 Gong。如果任务依赖聊天之外的信息、其他系统中的操作或可重复使用的工作流，就可以使用插件。</p> <blockquote> <p>图示：ChatGPT 插件目录展示 Google Drive、Slack 和 SharePoint 等已连接工具</p> </blockquote> <p>插件可用性取决于套餐、工作区设置和具体插件。更多信息请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">技能与插件</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"share-a-read-only-snapshot-of-a-codex-thread\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">分享 Codex 对话的只读快照</h2> <p>所有 Codex 套餐都可以在 macOS 版 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，为本地 Codex 对话创建只读快照。该快照不会让其他人获得你的项目或电脑访问权。</p> <p>分享前，请确认哪些人可以打开链接：</p> <ul> <li><strong>个人账户：</strong> 任何拥有链接的人都可以打开快照。</li> <li> <p><strong>工作区账户：</strong> 只有通过身份验证、属于创建快照的工作区的成员才能打开。你可以允许该工作区的所有成员访问，也可以限制为受邀人员和群组。工作区管理员可以关闭工作区分享链接。</p> </li> <li> <p>打开对话并选择 <strong>Share</strong>。如果支持斜杠命令，也可以使用 <code>/share</code>。</p> </li> <li>如果使用工作区账户，请在 <strong>Who has access</strong> 中选择允许整个工作区访问，或只允许 <strong>Only people and groups invited</strong>（受邀人员和群组）。选择仅限受邀者时，可以按电子邮件地址添加现有工作区成员，或选择工作区群组。</li> <li>等待快照上传完成，然后选择 <strong>Copy link</strong>。打开对话框会开始上传，但只有在你选择 <strong>Copy link</strong> 后，Codex 才会按照你选择的受众和接收者发布快照。</li> <li>打开复制的链接并检查分享视图，再将其发送给其他人。</li> </ul> <p>快照会记录分享时可用的受支持对话内容。之后的新消息和更改不会更新现有快照。</p> <p>共享快照可能包含用户可见消息、推理摘要、图片附件、智能体查看或生成的图片，以及文件更改（包括路径和差异）。它们不包含原对话的工具调用、Shell 命令或工具输入输出。</p> <p>Codex 会在上传快照前遮盖已知机密模式。发送链接前请检查分享视图，因为消息、图片或差异中仍可能包含文件路径等敏感内容。</p> <p>你不能从共享快照分叉出原始对话。你可以将快照作为附件导入新对话，并在其中引用。</p> <p>如需查看或撤销共享链接，请打开 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/#settings/DataControls\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 数据控制（需联网）</a>，然后选择 <strong>Shared links</strong>。</p> <p><a id=\"make-the-result-ready-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">让结果可以直接使用</h2> <p>把第一次得到的结果视作草稿，检查它、质疑它并继续改进。即使回答已经润色，也可能不完整或有误；在使用或分享前，请核实重要细节。</p> <p><strong>检查结果：</strong></p> <ul> <li>核对重要数字、名称、日期、引文和事实陈述。</li> <li>打开生成的文件，检查每个部分、标签页、幻灯片或页面。</li> <li>确认 ChatGPT 使用了正确且最新的源材料。</li> <li>查找缺失信息和缺乏依据的假设。</li> <li>如果结果未达到目标，请提出有针对性的修改要求。</li> </ul> <p>然后请 ChatGPT 对结果进行压力测试：</p> <ul> <li>“你使用了哪些来源？”</li> <li>“请为每项主要结论注明来源。”</li> <li>“你做了哪些假设？”</li> <li>“你有哪些信息无法访问？”</li> <li>“什么情况会改变你的建议？”</li> <li>“请对照原始文件检查这份结果。”</li> </ul> <p>如果 ChatGPT 无法访问某个来源或完成部分任务，请它明确说明。清楚指出缺口，比自信地猜测更容易补救。</p> <p>法律、金融、医疗、安全及其他高风险决策，需要适当的专家审查。请将 ChatGPT 用作辅助判断的工具，而不是替代专业人士。</p> <p><a id=\"next-steps\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">后续步骤</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-b90e41678b0234ad\"><strong>打开快速入门</strong><br>通过一个引导式首任务开始使用 ChatGPT。</a></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64\"><strong>了解提示写法</strong><br>学习如何为提问、完整成果和编程任务编写有效提示。</a></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-b81d7ecf0390ca3e\"><strong>个性化 ChatGPT</strong><br>设置偏好，并在对话之间保留有用的上下文。</a></p>","en":"<h1 id=\"use-chatgpt\">Use ChatGPT</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"go-from-idea-to-useful-result\">Go from idea to useful result</h2> <p>ChatGPT is an AI agent that you communicate with in natural language:</p> <ol> <li> <p>Start with a question, an idea, rough notes, a file, or a task you need to complete.</p> </li> <li> <p>Ask ChatGPT to explain information, develop ideas, draft content, research a topic, analyze materials, or create something new.</p> </li> <li> <p>Add the context and tools it needs, such as files, web search, projects, or plugins.</p> </li> <li> <p>Review the result, correct the direction, and ask for changes. You don't need a perfect first prompt or special commands.</p> </li> </ol> <h2 id=\"choose-how-you-want-to-work\">Choose how you want to work</h2> <p>Use Chat for a question or back-and-forth. Turn on Work in the switcher when you want ChatGPT to carry a larger task through to a reviewable result. Select Codex when you want developer views or more technical detail, especially for software development.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Choose</th> <th>When you want to</th> <th>Examples</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Chat</td> <td>Work through something with ChatGPT</td> <td>Ask a question, search the web, brainstorm, draft a message, compare options</td> </tr> <tr> <td>ChatGPT Work</td> <td>Define an outcome and get a reviewable result</td> <td>Create a deck, analyze files, draft a report, build a project plan</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex</td> <td>Use developer tools and see technical details</td> <td>Debug code, run tests, review a PR, implement a feature</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Use Chat to ask questions, brainstorm, draft or revise text, summarize files, compare options, or clarify a larger task. In Codex, point to <strong>New chat</strong>, then select <strong>Quick chat</strong> when that option is available.</p> <p>When you need a finished, reviewable result, switch to <strong>Work</strong> and describe what it should include. See <a href=\"#/article/a-2c7688c996bc9669\">Get started with ChatGPT Work</a> for example tasks, prompts, and best practices.</p> <h3 id=\"what-chatgpt-work-can-do\">What ChatGPT Work can do</h3> <p>ChatGPT Work can plan a task, gather context, use tools, and carry the work through to a result you can review.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT Work comparing vendors and producing a spreadsheet you can review.</p> </blockquote> <p>Ask it to:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Research and analyze information.</strong> Search the web, browse websites, compare sources, read files, analyze data, and summarize findings.</li> <li><strong>Use your files and tools.</strong> Bring in uploaded files, <a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">projects</a>, memories, ChatGPT Library, and installed <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">plugins</a>. Plugins can provide connected information, reusable workflows, and supported actions.</li> <li><strong>Create finished files.</strong> Draft and refine <a href=\"#/article/a-1186da4cb8c2d6e2\">documents, presentations, spreadsheets, and PDF files</a>. Review the result, ask for specific changes, and download the completed file.</li> <li><strong>Create visual and interactive work.</strong> Generate or edit <a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">images</a>, make interactive <a href=\"#/article/a-989576428b6123b7\">visualizations</a>, and build or share websites and apps with <a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Sites</a>.</li> <li><strong>Work across websites and apps.</strong> Use the <a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809\">browser</a> to research and interact with websites. In the desktop app, use the <a href=\"#/article/a-a7459570776840aa\">browser extension</a>, <a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use</a>, and <a href=\"#/article/a-c302b8efa03eab38\">appshots</a> when those features are available.</li> <li><strong>Run code and review technical work.</strong> Run code and shell commands, analyze data, inspect files, <a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">review code</a>, and work with repositories your selected environment can access.</li> <li><strong>Delegate and continue longer tasks.</strong> Split independent work across <a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">subagents</a>, follow their progress, and keep <a href=\"#/article/a-916e12c5bba5b9cc\">long-running work</a> active.</li> <li><strong>Repeat useful workflows.</strong> Set up <a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">scheduled tasks</a> for recurring work and use <a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">skills</a> to reuse a workflow.</li> <li><strong>Talk through a task.</strong> On supported plans in the desktop app, use <a href=\"#/article/a-3b6d55bd01328040\">ChatGPT Voice</a> to start work, check progress, or change direction.</li> </ul> <p>Features depend on your plan, platform, region, rollout, and workspace settings. Your workspace administrator can control access to ChatGPT Work, plugins, browser use, and network access. ChatGPT Work and Codex share <a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">usage limits</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"choose-cloud-or-local-work\">Choose cloud or local work</h3> <p>On the web, ChatGPT Work runs in a managed cloud environment. In the desktop app, you may also be able to choose where a task runs:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Cloud:</strong> Run work in an isolated hosted environment. A task can keep going after you close the desktop app and continue from the web or mobile app. Cloud work can use uploaded files, connected tools, and approved websites.</li> <li><strong>Work locally:</strong> Use files, apps, or the browser on your computer. Local work is available in the desktop app when enabled for your account or workspace.</li> </ul> <p>ChatGPT shows its progress and pauses when it needs information or approval. Review consequential actions before approving them, and check the final result before you use or share it.</p> <p><a id=\"compare-work-mode-and-codex-on-desktop\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"compare-chatgpt-work-and-codex-on-desktop\">Compare ChatGPT Work and Codex on desktop</h3> <p>ChatGPT Work and Codex have overlapping capabilities. If you prefer Codex, you can keep using it for research, documents, presentations, and other knowledge work. When both are available to you, the desktop app changes the interface and how the agent presents its work.</p> <p><a id=\"detailed-comparison\"></a> <strong>Detailed comparison</strong></p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Difference</th> <th>ChatGPT in Desktop app</th> <th>Codex in Desktop app</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Where to start</td> <td>Select <strong>ChatGPT</strong>, then switch to <strong>Work</strong></td> <td>Select <strong>Codex</strong> in the product selector</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Chats you see</td> <td>See chats started with Chat on web and mobile, plus ChatGPT Work chats</td> <td>Focus on Codex chats and development projects</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Quick chat</td> <td>Not available</td> <td>When available, access ChatGPT chats from web and mobile in Codex</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Technical detail</td> <td>Hide technical details like Git or shell commands</td> <td>See developer details, including diff and review views</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Agent communication</td> <td>Prefers nontechnical language and finished outputs</td> <td>Can include technical and implementation details</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Pull requests pane</td> <td>Not available when using ChatGPT Work</td> <td>Available when enabled</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h3 id=\"talk-to-chatgpt-naturally\">Talk to ChatGPT naturally</h3> <p>Write as if you were explaining the request to a helpful colleague. State what you want to accomplish, add the details that change the answer, and describe the format you need. Your first prompt is only a starting point—you can add context or refine the result with follow-up messages.</p> <p><strong>Start simple:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Help me plan a 30-minute team meeting about our new customer feedback process.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Add context:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Help me plan a 30-minute team meeting about our new customer feedback process. The audience is a customer support team that hasn't seen the process before. Include five minutes for questions and end with clear next steps.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Choose a format:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Create a 30-minute agenda for a customer support team that hasn't seen our new customer feedback process before. Include five minutes for questions, end with clear next steps, and format it so I can paste it into a calendar invitation.\n</code></pre> <p>You can continue with simple directions such as:</p> <ul> <li>“Make this shorter.”</li> <li>“Give me three different approaches.”</li> <li>“What assumptions are you making?”</li> <li>“Ask me questions before you continue.”</li> </ul> <p>Learn more about <a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64\">prompting</a>, or take the <a href=\"https://academy.openai.com/home/courses/ai-foundations-juzjs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AI Foundations course (online)</a> for guided practice.</p> <h2 id=\"bring-the-right-context-into-chatgpt\">Bring the right context into ChatGPT</h2> <p>Give ChatGPT the information, tools, and instructions that matter to the task. You don't need to provide everything—include the context that changes what a good result looks like.</p> <h3 id=\"keep-related-work-in-a-project\">Keep related work in a project</h3> <p>Projects help you organize ChatGPT around a topic, goal, or ongoing body of work. Keep related chats, files, and instructions in one project when the work will continue over time or depend on the same context. <a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">Learn more about projects.</a></p> <h3 id=\"attach-files\">Attach files</h3> <p>You can upload or attach documents, presentations, spreadsheets, PDF files, images, and data exports. Use them when you want ChatGPT to:</p> <ul> <li>Summarize or compare them.</li> <li>Find patterns or inconsistencies.</li> <li>Extract, clean, or reorganize information.</li> <li>Use them as source material for a new file.</li> </ul> <p>When ChatGPT creates a file, open the preview and check its contents. You can then ask for changes without starting over. Learn more about <a href=\"#/article/a-1186da4cb8c2d6e2\">working with files</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"connect-tools-with-plugins\">Connect tools with plugins</h3> <p>Plugins can connect ChatGPT to the tools and information you use for work, such as Google Drive, SharePoint, Salesforce, or Gong. Use them when a task depends on information outside the chat, actions in another system, or a repeatable workflow.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT plugin directory showing connected tools such as Google Drive, Slack, and SharePoint.</p> </blockquote> <p>Plugin availability depends on your plan, workspace settings, and the plugin itself. Learn more about <a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">skills and plugins</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"share-a-read-only-snapshot-of-a-codex-thread\">Share a read-only snapshot of a Codex thread</h2> <p>On all Codex plans, you can create a read-only snapshot of a local Codex thread in the ChatGPT desktop app for macOS. The snapshot doesn't give other people access to your project or computer.</p> <p>Before sharing, check who can open the link:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Personal account:</strong> Anyone with the link can open the snapshot.</li> <li> <p><strong>Workspace account:</strong> Only authenticated members of the workspace that created the snapshot can open it. You can allow everyone in that workspace or restrict access to invited people and groups. A workspace administrator can turn off workspace share links.</p> </li> <li> <p>Open the thread and select <strong>Share</strong>. You can also use <code>/share</code> where slash commands are available.</p> </li> <li>For a workspace account, use <strong>Who has access</strong> to choose everyone in your workspace or <strong>Only people and groups invited</strong>. For invited-only access, add existing workspace members by email or choose workspace groups.</li> <li>Wait for the snapshot to finish uploading, then select <strong>Copy link</strong>. Opening the dialog starts the upload, but Codex publishes the snapshot only when you select <strong>Copy link</strong>, using your chosen audience and recipients.</li> <li>Open the copied link and review the shared view before sending it to anyone.</li> </ul> <p>A snapshot captures the supported thread content available when you share it. Later messages and changes don't update the existing snapshot.</p> <p>Shared snapshots can include user-visible messages, reasoning summaries, image attachments, images viewed or generated by the agent, and file changes, including paths and diffs. They don't include the original thread's tool calls, shell commands, or tool input or output.</p> <p>Codex redacts known secret patterns before uploading a snapshot. Review the shared view before sending its link because sensitive content, including file paths, may remain in messages, images, or diffs.</p> <p>You can't fork the original thread from a shared snapshot. You can import the snapshot as an attachment and refer to it in a new thread.</p> <p>To view or revoke a shared link, open <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/#settings/DataControls\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT data controls (online)</a> and select <strong>Shared links</strong>.</p> <h2 id=\"make-the-result-ready-to-use\">Make the result ready to use</h2> <p>Treat the first result as a draft you can inspect, challenge, and improve. A polished response can still be incomplete or wrong, so review the details that matter before you use or share it.</p> <p><strong>Check the work:</strong></p> <ul> <li>Verify important numbers, names, dates, quotes, and claims.</li> <li>Open generated files and inspect every section, tab, slide, or page.</li> <li>Confirm that ChatGPT used the correct and most current source material.</li> <li>Look for missing information and unsupported assumptions.</li> <li>Ask for focused revisions when the result misses the goal.</li> </ul> <p>Then ask ChatGPT to pressure-test the result:</p> <ul> <li>“What sources did you use for this?”</li> <li>“Cite the source for each major claim.”</li> <li>“What assumptions did you make?”</li> <li>“What information were you unable to access?”</li> <li>“What would change your recommendation?”</li> <li>“Check this result against the original files.”</li> </ul> <p>If ChatGPT couldn't access a source or complete part of the task, ask it to say so plainly. An explicit gap is easier to address than a confident guess.</p> <p>Legal, financial, medical, security, and other high-stakes decisions require appropriate expert review. Use ChatGPT to support informed judgment, not replace it.</p> <h2 id=\"next-steps\">Next steps</h2> <p>a]:min-w-0 [&amp;&gt;a]:no-underline\"&gt; <a href=\"#/article/a-b90e41678b0234ad\"><strong>Open the quickstart</strong><br>Start using ChatGPT with a guided first task.</a></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64\"><strong>Learn about prompting</strong><br>Write useful prompts for questions, finished work, and coding tasks.</a></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-b81d7ecf0390ca3e\"><strong>Personalize ChatGPT</strong><br>Set preferences and carry useful context across chats.</a></p>"};
